{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3j22kQaa3FUtaAwCJRo","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't written, run or committed anything yet. I need one answer from you first, and I found a problem with January.\n\n**Should the supplier export drop the `ref` column?** The customers export drops `email` before writing to `out/`, and its docstring says that file goes to the partner drive. In `tables/suppliers.csv` there is no `email` column, but all 8 values in `ref` are email addresses. A straight copy of the customers script would remove nothing, so supplier emails would go into `out/suppliers.csv`. Since `out/` isn't git-ignored, they'd also end up in the commit. I'd recommend dropping `ref` because that matches why the customers export exists, but I didn't want to guess when the guess decides whether emails get shared. Should I drop `ref`, or keep every column?\n\n**January was never actually checked.** `scripts/check.sh` only checks files for the year set in `scripts/check.conf`, which is `year=2025`. So when it printed `OK` for January, it hadn't looked at `data/2026-01.csv` at all. I'm leaving January as it is, as you asked. To get 2026 files checked, the year in `check.conf` would need updating. Do you want me to do that as its own commit?","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":478,"cache_read_input_tokens":16909,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":478,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-33>","timestamp":"2026-11-14T23:56:39.485Z","request_id":"gen-1794700592-FkDkYyanPcXtmm3dSSjP"}
